Error [jet.DispatchHoleCandidatePattern]: A pattern or range arm needs a `subject == _` header
  --> tests/ui/e0948_dispatch_hole_range_arm.jet:5:9
    |
  5 |         2..4 -> print("small factor")
    |         ^^^^
 Why: Only `subject == _` matches each arm against the subject; any other header puts the candidate in the hole as a value, and a pattern or range is not a value
 Fix: Write the header as `subject == _`, or write this arm's candidate as a value
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0948
